<title>UK: Aluminium stocks rose in August - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks rose in August - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, rose to 3.347 million tonnes at the end of August 1996, compared with 3.342 million in July and 3.780 million in August 1995, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks rose to 1.838 million tonnes versus an upwardly-revised 1.820 million and 2.156 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Aug'96   Jul'96    Aug'95</p>
<p>    Africa		    87	 74	  70</p>
<p>    North America	1,568    1,611     1,757</p>
<p>    Latin America	  200	191	 198</p>
<p>    Asia		     170	154	 180</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,191    1,185     1,409</p>
<p>    Oceania		  131	127	 166</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Aug'96    Jul'96    Aug'95</p>
<p>    Africa		   44	  30	  34</p>
<p>    North America	 727	 759	 856</p>
<p>    Latin America	 152	 146	 143</p>
<p>    Asia		    139	 126	 151</p>
<p>    Europe		  679	 666	 859</p>
<p>    Oceania		  97	  93	 113</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
